"## Summary\n\nAgent-core follow-up 49: F30-01's agent half under D-155 (review r29's H-1 and M-1), and F48-01 under D-156.\n- **Session:** launched 21:46 EST on 2026-11-03, and delivered at 23:48.\n- **Model:** codex `gpt-6-astra`.\n- **Size:** 6 commits and 13 owned files, +1,559/\u221241.\n- **Checks:**\n  - merge-tree clean on current `main`; prepush-scan clean; owned-check passes.\n  - **The orchestrator reran these** on a scratch tree: current `main` (`b56c0b36`, after #451) with members 21 and this branch merged in. All pass:\n    - `make -f mk/node.mk node-lint node-test node-test-integration node-build`;\n    - the review proofs r16 to r29 in `node/agent`, `fvpn-agent`, `node/enforce` and `node/watchdog`, including r29's four;\n    - the lock's consumers: `go test ./node/updater/... ./node/nodelock/... ./node/internal/nodelock/...`;\n    - `go test ./tests/handover/...` and the committed-evidence tests;\n    - `make go-lint`, `go vet ./...`, gofmt and `git diff --check`.\n- **Scope:** one ordinary lab in the lane's own prefix, with no rerun and no reservation. It waited 228 s for other lanes' runs first. Zero owned Docker objects at the end.\n\n**The orchestrator's reading.**\n- **Three confirmed defects, each fixed, each with its proof failing before and passing after.** Review r29's imported proof file stays byte-identical, and its two Held proofs pass throughout.\n- **r29 H-1, F30-01's agent half under D-155** (`2ec714aa`).\n  - **Before:** a candidate agent started by its parent updater, while that updater held `update.lock`, ran its boot recovery once. It latched `recovery_required` for good, even after the lock was released. The one-shot recovery dates from #25.\n  - **Now:** the agent probes the lock once, defers recovery while the parent holds it, and retries on later Steps. It serves after the commit. Terminal failures (exits 1 and 2, missing config) stay terminal.\n  - **While deferred,** D-053's health attestation, D-064's probe exception, lease renewal and watchdog publication stay active. Central sees `applying` with `recovery_required`, and may issue a zero-grant lease.\n- **r29 M-1** (`a56a17b7`, `4a541c55`).\n  - **Before:** recovery waited synchronously for this same agent's checkpoint or health attestation, so Boot ran out its own deadline.\n  - **Now:** recovery is one tracked child, owned by the engine's run context. A new child gets a 250 ms first wait; later Steps poll without waiting, at most one dispatch a second. Stopping the agent cancels the child's process group and joins it.\n  - **Proof:** real updater recoveries from all three crashed stages, blocked, switched and checking, keep the agent running.\n- **F48-01 under D-156** (`08af6925`).\n  - **Before:** in a same-boot restart, a watchdog pass between the successor's startup heartbeat and its adoption of the retained ruleset withdrew the verified rules. It came from #429's early uncertainty publication for review r22's M-3.\n  - **Now:** the successor publishes a pending-adoption receipt that keeps the predecessor's original heartbeat age and kernel deadline, with no serving or baseline claim. A second startup cannot refresh it.\n  - **Bounded:** a stalled successor is still withdrawn at the next watchdog poll after the old staleness limit (by default, 30 s stale plus up to 10 s of polling), or at the kernel deadline, whichever comes first. A wrong-boot, future, stale, malformed or unverified predecessor gets ordinary uncertainty, and a refused adoption takes the baseline. r22's M-3 is kept.\n  - **Agent and watchdog ship together.** An older watchdog still withdraws early, which is the conservative side.\n  - **Proofs:** the watchdog runs between startup and adoption in three cases, adopt, stall and refuse; a repeated startup cannot renew the receipt; the receipt keeps the original bounds. Before this change, the deterministic interleaving failed.\n- **D-156 is the orchestrator's provisional decision.**\n- **The lab:** 13 of 13 ordinary scenarios on one attempt, including D087/D104's expiry correlation.\n- **Not covered here:**\n  - no ordinary lab scenario starts a candidate under a parent-held `update.lock`. Devstack's acceptance run on this merge exercises the real update path;\n  - arm64 is cross-compiled, not run.\n- **F30-01 closes** only when an acceptance run passes `lease-expiry` with the nightly quarantine entry removed. Devstack's next follow-up starts on this merge for exactly that, which is this follow-up's one request.\n- **Carried:** F31-01, F17-01 and r28's management-loss note.\n"
